From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: turing-rk1: export block devices over USB with ums

The RK1 is a compute module, so its device-mode USB is not a front-panel
socket an operator can reach: usb_host0_xhci is the module's only
OTG-capable controller, and where it lands is the carrier board's
decision. On a cluster carrier that is a management controller, which
can write the module's eMMC and nothing else -- an NVMe on the M.2 slot
behind pcie3x4 is invisible to it. The result is a disk u-boot
enumerates perfectly well but that no host can address.

`ums` closes that gap. It exports any block device u-boot can reach as
USB mass storage, so `ums 0 nvme 0` puts the M.2 disk in front of
whatever sits on the OTG port and it is written, imaged, or fsck'd with
ordinary host tools, with no OS on the module. The pieces it leans on
are already here: CONFIG_NVME_PCI and CONFIG_PCIE_DW_ROCKCHIP enumerate
the disk, and the gadget side is the one CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB already
uses.

Drop the CMD_SETEXPR override in the same change, restoring the
default-y expression evaluator. Writing an image by hand needs it to
turn a loaded ${filesize} into the block count `nvme write` takes, and
it is the one arithmetic primitive a scripted flashing session cannot
work around.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig b/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
index 0b3efec2..347a36a2 100644
--- a/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
+++ b/configs/turing-rk1-rk3588_defconfig
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ CONFIG_CMD_PCI=y
 # CONFIG_CMD_SATA is not set
 CONFIG_CMD_USB=y
 CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB=y
-# CONFIG_CMD_SETEXPR is not set
+CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPPUT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_TFTPSRV=y
 CONFIG_CMD_REGULATOR=y
-- 
2.43.0
